PROPOSAL ONLY (the late frame, docs/measurements/2026-11-20-late-frame.md). Not in a build that
a trial, the gate or a verdict uses: scripts/build-compositor.sh does not know it (it is in a
folder of its own, and it is not a trial-*.patch). Whether it goes into the measured build is
for the owner to decide: it changes the path that is measured.

A patch against gst-wayland-display (https://github.com/games-on-whales/gst-wayland-display,
MIT License), commit 1301f86, on top of the four measured patches in scripts/patches
(render-on-commit, cursor-messages, windows, dialogs, in that order). The lines of context are
from that project and from those patches.

What it changes: `State::create_frame` waits for the renderer to have drawn the frame before it
asks for the copy into the element's buffer.

Why: with `memory:CUDAMemory` frames the copy is `CuMemcpy2DAsync` on a CUDA stream, out of the
buffer the renderer draws into. The renderer has only been told to start by then (`glFlush` and
a fence), and nothing orders the CUDA copy after its work. Now and then the copy runs first and
takes what the buffer held before: the picture of the frame before. The frame that was drawn
for a commit then goes out without what was committed. Where the picture stands still, the
"render on commit" mode sends the next frame only two frame intervals later, and that one
shows it: about 24 ms late at 85 frames a second. Whoever asked for the frame already waits
for the same fence (comp/mod.rs, "we need to wait before giving a hardware buffer to
gstreamer"), but only after the copy has been asked for; with this patch that later wait
comes back at once. The frames in system memory and as DMABuf are not changed in what they
show (the first is read back through the renderer, the second was waited for already).

diff --git a/wayland-display-core/src/comp/rendering.rs b/wayland-display-core/src/comp/rendering.rs
index 22619ab..81c7286 100644
--- a/wayland-display-core/src/comp/rendering.rs
+++ b/wayland-display-core/src/comp/rendering.rs
@@ -86,6 +86,17 @@ impl State {
             [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0],
         )?;
 
+        // Nothing orders the copy into the element's buffer after the renderer's work: with
+        // CUDA it is a copy on a CUDA stream of what the renderer draws into, and the
+        // renderer has only been told to start. A copy that runs first takes the picture of
+        // the frame before. So the drawing is waited for here, before the copy is asked for.
+        // (Whoever asked for the frame waits for the same point before handing the buffer
+        // on; that wait then comes back at once.)
+        render_output_result
+            .sync
+            .wait()
+            .map_err(|_| OutputDamageTrackerError::Rendering(GlesError::SyncInterrupted))?;
+
         match self
             .output_buffer
             .clone()
